Leak fix proved by re-running the L3 mutation (`SET LOCAL lock_timeout` cut):
  before: test failed at 20012ms AND "Hook timed out in 10000ms",
          4 K026 companies left behind on the fixture DB, row still locked.
  after:  test failed at 8078ms, no hook timeout, 0 rows left behind.
The holder's own `idle_in_transaction_session_timeout = '8s'` is what frees the
row — vitest abandons a timed-out test without unwinding it, so a `finally`
alone never runs. 8s > the route's 5s lock_timeout, so it cannot fire while the
code is correct.

assertTxUsable(): no test. The flag it reads is set only by a failed
`ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT`, and this route runs no savepoint before the lock, so
the branch is unreachable today — added for fidelity to creditNoteLock, not to
fix a reachable defect.
